{"type":"text","timestamp":1794365360235,"sessionID":"ses_e378656c8ffeGtYdaPC77uGrl1","part":{"id":"prt_1c882884c001jurZXffxiPokQM","messageID":"msg_1c8826a78001bWb62i5MR7uv2T","sessionID":"ses_e378656c8ffeGtYdaPC77uGrl1","type":"text","text":"Done. Built the multi-author blog on top of the existing scaffold.\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`): SQLite storage under `./data`, token sessions with Bearer auth, all endpoints (`register`, `login`, `me`/`logout`, paged/filterable `GET /api/posts`, CRUD on posts, admin toggle). Enforcement of the rules: anyone reads, author-only edits/deletes, taken-down posts hidden from list and 404 to non-admins, `excerpt` = first 200 chars with newlines collapsed, `updated_at` bumps on updates, admin password from `ADMIN_PASSWORD` (admin login disabled when unset/empty).\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/`): React + TypeScript with Tailwind CSS v4 (via `@tailwindcss/vite`), custom hash-free router, and pages for sign-in/register, the post list (search, tag/author filters, paging), post page (plain text with paragraphs, admin take-down button, author edit/delete with confirmation), and the editor (title, content, comma-separated tags, surfaces API validation messages).\n\nVerified end-to-end: full API flow (register/login/auth checks, permissions, filtering, paging, take-down visibility, admin disabled), `npm ci && npm run build` succeeds, and the backend serves both the API and the built SPA.\n\nNote: I added a `taken_down` boolean to the post JSON (frontend needs it to render the admin button), which is additive to the required fields.","time":{"start":1794365360204,"end":1794365360208}}}
